TYPE 1 — BRACKET MATCHING
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

When to use:
→ Check if brackets are valid
→ Find unmatched brackets
→ Minimum additions/removals to make valid

The idea: push opening brackets onto the stack.
When you see a closing bracket, pop and check if it matches.
At the end, anything left on the stack is unmatched.

TEMPLATE:

bool isValid(string s) {
    stack<char> st;
    for (char c : s) {
        if (c == '(' || c == '[' || c == '{') {
            st.push(c);
        } else {
            if (st.empty()) return false;
            if (c == ')' && st.top() != '(') return false;
            if (c == ']' && st.top() != '[') return false;
            if (c == '}' && st.top() != '{') return false;
            st.pop();
        }
    }
    return st.empty();
}
EXAMPLE — Valid Parentheses
https://leetcode.com/problems/valid-parentheses

Directly apply the template above.

EXAMPLE — Minimum Remove to Make Valid Parentheses
https://leetcode.com/problems/minimum-remove-to-make-valid-parentheses

Push the INDEX (not the char) of unmatched '(' onto the stack.
When you see ')': if stack is non-empty → pop (matched pair).
                  if stack is empty    → mark ')' for removal.
After the loop: all indices left in the stack are unmatched '(' → remove them.
string minRemoveToMakeValid(string s) {
    stack<int> st;
    set<int> remove;
    for (int i = 0; i < s.size(); i++) {
        if (s[i] == '(') {
            st.push(i);
        } else if (s[i] == ')') {
            if (!st.empty()) st.pop();
            else remove.insert(i);   // unmatched ')'
        }
    }
    while (!st.empty()) { remove.insert(st.top()); st.pop(); }  // unmatched '('
    string res;
    for (int i = 0; i < s.size(); i++)
        if (!remove.count(i)) res += s[i];
    return res;
}
EXAMPLE — Longest Valid Parentheses
https://leetcode.com/problems/longest-valid-parentheses

Push indices. When a ')' matches a '(', pop it.
The longest valid substring = gap between remaining unmatched indices.
Push -1 as a sentinel at the start so the first valid char has a boundary.
int longestValidParentheses(string s) {
    stack<int> st;
    st.push(-1);   // sentinel
    int ans = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < s.size(); i++) {
        if (s[i] == '(') {
            st.push(i);
        } else {
            st.pop();
            if (st.empty()) st.push(i);   // new boundary
            else ans = max(ans, i - st.top());
        }
    }
    return ans;
}
