HOW TO IDENTIFY WHICH TYPE — DECISION GUIDE
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Read the problem. Ask these questions in order:

Does it involve brackets, parentheses, or nested structures?
→ YES → Type 1 (Bracket Matching)
Count unmatched → track indices on stack.
Nested decoding → push state on '[', restore on ']'.

Does it ask for next/previous greater or smaller element?
Or involve histograms, trapped water, or span of a value?
→ YES → Type 2 (Monotonic Stack)
Next GREATER → decreasing stack (pop when current > top).
Next SMALLER → increasing stack (pop when current < top).

Does it involve evaluating a mathematical expression?
→ YES → Type 3 (Expression Evaluation)
Postfix (RPN) → push numbers, apply on operator.
Infix (+,-,*,/) → defer + and -, compute * and / immediately.

Do elements cancel, destroy, or modify each other?
→ YES → Type 4 (Stack Simulation)

